    "summary": "Think you need a scan to figure out what's causing your pain? Not always. \n\nAUT physiotherapy lecturer David Toomey says scans don't always tell the full story. Many people have changes on scans that cause no pain at all, while others experience pain that a scan can't fully explain. \n\nPain is complex, which is why understanding the person, not just the picture, is often the most important part of treatment. \n\n#PainScience #Physiotherapy #HealthMyths",
